atlas institutional-product-contracts

architecture institutional-product-contracts
  canonical_name ProductContracts
  owns ProductContract
  owns CapabilityBinding
  consumes SurfaceIR
  consumes DelegationEnvelope
  consumes SemanticProgramIR
  consumes Authority
  consumes WorkState
  publishes ProductContract
  publishes CapabilityBinding
  family institutional
  domain Institution / Downstream product
  layer surface
  semantic_question What can a person in this downstream organization actually see, filter, run and approve, and which existing route or function realizes it?
  purpose Bind an existing application's real routes, calculations, reports and jobs to the semantic estate without replacing them, so a downstream product gets more capability while its working software keeps running.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ProductContract
  node_types BoundDomainProduct
  node_types CapabilityBinding
  node_types DomainAction
  node_types ReportContract
  node_types FilterContract
  edge_types binds
  edge_types realized_by
  edge_types projected_into
  edge_types requests_review
  internal_calculus a delegated host first verifies exact institution admission, then BonfyreUpper90 resolves the session actor to one native AuthorityGraph-backed named role and scope before compiling an HTMX product closure
  internal_calculus Upper90 leadership is a live parent delegation to JRSS internal administration, AI Loss administration, and Leads Demo administration; the child grammar is compiled at render and submit time from the parent edge rather than copied as a child grant
  internal_calculus BonfyreUpper90 closure emits only verified estate, actor, inherited state, and scope coordinates for CMS, Studio, ForeignTwin, and MCP carrier compilation; it does not emit client records or replace any downstream owner
  internal_calculus a protected product request carries an opaque reference into a registered upper90-private WorkGraph family; the native product returns a durable review mission and does not invoke a JRSS or AI Loss legacy route
  internal_calculus the standalone AI Loss saved-projection compiler reads the authored product pack and CUE projection law into inert Query IR; its optional operating view summarizes the current pure close-consequence receipt without applying it
  invariant a binding makes an existing route visible to the estate; it does not replace or reimplement that route
  invariant a downstream product is expressed in its own domain language, never in Powers, Partner names or engine vocabulary
  invariant a bound domain product terminates in a concrete user experience; attachment to the institutional graph alone is not a binding
  invariant a report contract records its filters, because a report without its filter set is not reproducible
  invariant an existing report or ad-hoc report builder is preserved as a capability, never dropped as legacy
  invariant a binding declares its effect class from QUERY, DERIVE or EFFECT before it may be planned
  invariant a binding carries the full semantic lineage defined by PreservationBoundary, sufficient to reconstruct the original behavior
  invariant scheduled and background behavior is bound as product capability; having no screen is not being absent
  invariant a downstream product presents named domain sections, never capability identifiers
  invariant added capability sits beside existing capability and never retires it
  invariant exact institution admission is not a product role or object-level closure; both gates must be current before any downstream section or request appears
  invariant a JRSS, AI Loss, Leads, or Upper90 product request never reads, displays, or mutates a client record merely from its opaque reference
  invariant a PhysicalCarrier section in a delegated private Studio resolves only through the already-admitted estate CMS namespace; a visual/mobile handoff cannot become a second disclosure path, select a sibling namespace, or authorize a foreign/device/payment effect
  invariant revoking Upper90 leadership removes every child product aperture it supplied immediately; a child role never climbs to leadership or crosses siblings
  invariant a saved AI Loss projection declares its basis, fields, filters, scope, policy, and materialization target but grants no table, financial, scheduling, or external effect authority
  invariant Leads remains DEMO-only: its private product may use synthetic/replayed scenario state and proposal economics but cannot read LIVE client state or initiate a third-party effect
  forbidden_inference a route being bound -> that route being safe to change
  forbidden_inference a compiled function existing for a domain -> the downstream product needing to adopt it
  forbidden_inference engine capability -> downstream user visibility
  forbidden_inference a legacy implementation -> disposable functionality
  forbidden_inference an AI Loss saved projection or close frontier -> an executed query, approved close, financial write, or live private product binding
  forbidden_inference repetition across bindings -> those bindings being one capability
  forbidden_inference a valid Aurekai session, institution grant, or role in one managed estate -> a role, scope, or data closure in another estate
  interacts institutional-root
  interacts delegation-model
  interacts surface
  interacts preservation-boundary
  interacts authority-graph
  interacts work-graph
  interacts web-address-edge
  interacts close-consequence
  source_path cmd/BonfyreUpper90/src/main.c
  source_path packs/upper90/ai-loss-projection.cue
  source_path packs/upper90/implementations/ai-loss-operating-estate.mjs
  source_path packs/upper90/implementations/ai-loss-projection-compile.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path deploy/nginx/aurekai-surfaces.conf
  witness cmd/BonfyreUpper90/tests/private_estate_smoke.sh
  witness packs/upper90/implementations/ai-loss-native.test.mjs proves pack-derived contract and report bases, authored CUE vocabulary, inert projection IR and explicit refusals, plus pure close receipt semantics
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/private_estate_surface_test.sh proves two independent gates, exact JRSS scope, WorkGraph review creation, cross-client form refusal, no protocol/RO-Crate discovery, and role/client revocation
  source_lineage Generation-10 product topology separation, 2026-08-26
  source_lineage route and report census of JRSSv1 and AiLtd_Loss, 2026-08-25

interaction ai-loss-close-consequence-enters-operating-view
  source close-consequence
  destination institutional-product-contracts
  relation read-only-pure-receipt-summary
  preserves named AI Loss namespace, source reachability, resolved and unevaluable counts, under- and over-allocation counts and amounts, and the explicit no-effect fact
  drops database credentials, client payment rows, approval authority, financial effects, and any inference from an unreachable source
  forbidden_inference an operating-view summary -> an approved or performed close, a live private product route, or an authority to execute the saved projection
  invalidates_on AI Loss product pack, close-consequence law, obligation source, or projection CUE policy changes
  witness packs/upper90/implementations/ai-loss-native.test.mjs
  binding packs/upper90/implementations/ai-loss-operating-estate.mjs
  binding scripts/product_close_consequence.mjs

interaction delegated-product-compiles-private-review-work
  source institutional-product-contracts
  destination work-graph
  relation scope-bounded-review-mission
  preserves named downstream estate, native role, scope reference, request kind, opaque reference token, AuthorityGraph admission, WorkGraph mission/node identifiers, and the fact that no legacy effect occurred
  drops client record contents, cross-client closure, card charge, payment/split/horse mutation, external contact, generic paid-tier authority, provider credentials, and all inferred facts from the opaque reference
  forbidden_inference a durable review mission -> approval, client mutation, legacy-route invocation, financial settlement, or authority to perform the requested effect
  invalidates_on role assignment/revocation, AuthorityGraph edge, requested estate/scope/kind, or WorkGraph routing-family changes
  witness cmd/BonfyreUpper90/tests/private_estate_smoke.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/private_estate_surface_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreUpper90/src/main.c
  binding engine/core/src/workgraph.c

interaction delegated-product-renders-private-closure
  source institutional-product-contracts
  destination web-address-edge
  relation host-admitted-role-scope-htmx-projection
  preserves exact protected host, active institution admission, session actor identifier, named product role, scope reference, HTML representation, and no-store/noindex policy
  drops machine-carrier publication, RO-Crate/Zarr/feed/protocol discovery, generic Matrix public fallback, cross-client role names, client records, and private request bodies from the edge
  forbidden_inference a protected hostname or signed-in account -> a publicly enumerable product surface or a readable client closure
  invalidates_on host-to-estate map, institution grant, role assignment, session revocation, representation policy, or protected-edge route changes
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/private_estate_surface_test.sh
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  binding deploy/nginx/aurekai-surfaces.conf

interaction delegated-product-compiles-cms-carrier
  source institutional-product-contracts
  destination web-address-edge
  relation closure-derived-private-cms-namespace
  preserves exact protected host, active institution admission, current session actor, native Upper90 estate, one owner-returned scope coordinate, registered CMS type grammar, and the native CMS row namespace only
  drops browser-selected namespace or scope, generic actor CMS namespace, sibling-estate rows, client record contents not deliberately authored into the CMS, public notes/routes, protocol publication, and all effect authority beyond the CMS owner's validated create/update operation
  forbidden_inference a current JRSS, AI Loss, Leads, or Upper90 closure -> authority to read another delegated estate's CMS rows or to publish a private CMS row publicly
  invalidates_on protected host mapping, institution grant, Upper90 role/scope assignment, session revocation, CMS namespace contract, or registered CMS grammar changes
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/private_estate_surface_test.sh creates a native JRSS wiki page under private:jrss:stable:cedar and proves the same admitted actor cannot see it through the AI Loss private CMS host; it further proves Upper90 leadership inherits a distinct private:jrss:institution:jrss CMS namespace rather than silently unioning the direct child scope
  binding cmd/BonfyreUpper90/src/main.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/main.c

interaction delegated-product-compiles-private-studio
  source institutional-product-contracts
  destination web-address-edge
  relation closure-derived-multi-owner-human-workroom
  preserves exact protected host, active institution admission, current session actor, native Upper90 estate and scope, Upper90 durable review-work grammar, CMS private namespace coordinate, ForeignTwin private receipt/body root coordinate, HTML/HTMX representation, and no-store/noindex policy only
  drops global Studio/operator surfaces, global finance/model/Fleming/Frappe state, browser-selected estate or namespace, sibling-estate content, public machine carrier publication, raw client records, arbitrary private body enumeration, and all effect authority beyond the individual native owners
  forbidden_inference a delegated /studio address -> a user may open the global Aurekai Studio or read a client plane that no named owner admitted
  invalidates_on protected host mapping, institution grant, Upper90 role/scope assignment, session revocation, owner carrier contract, or private-route disclosure policy changes
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/private_estate_surface_test.sh asserts the JRSS Studio contains native Stable Owner work and only CMS/ForeignTwin routes from private:jrss:stable:cedar while refusing global Institution Studio/financial output/raw JSON
  binding cmd/BonfyreUpper90/src/main.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreCMS/src/main.c
